# boot-vcsession-task127.log — task 127 (display arc M3: the VC-boot +
# dispman client) validation evidence.  Four boots of the full chain
# (SWBL shim -> genuine BB5 entry -> NLoader -> Linux e7:~#) with the
# QEMU MeSSI VC responder on (MESSI_RESPONDER=1, MESSI_DEBUG=1), each
# running tools/vc_session.c through /dev/bcm2727-vchi (never /dev/mem):
#
#   [1] poll mode, TCG        (cmdline vchi-bcm2727.poll=1)
#   [2] IRQ mode, TCG         (default; ICU 201, pair enables on)
#   [3] poll mode, -icount    (cmdline vchi-bcm2727.poll=1)
#   [4] IRQ mode, -icount     (default)
#
# All four print SESSION PASS: the §9 boot session driven from image
# files (stage-1 sentinel exchange, loader + firmware cmd-0x42 uploads
# with the magic-framed headers, the final count==3/answer==1), then
# the §10 service cycle (connect echo, DISP 0x10 update start with the
# captured handle, 0x17 element op with change-mask + rects, 0x11
# submit, the UPDH completion drain), plus the mid-session bad-CRC
# probe (the §8.4 rejection — SEND -EIO, 500 ms of silence, session
# recovers on the next exchange).  Every exchange is logged by the
# client with its wire-frame bytes and interpretation; the interleaved
# 'messi:' lines are the model trace.
#
# Synthetic image set (deterministic: ASCII banner, then (i*131+7)&0xFF):
#   loader.bin  8272 B (0x2050 — the real img1/img2 length, §7.3)
#               md5 53326b7d4317e532ae5fb35e8c857a30
#   fw.bin     16384 B (synthetic size)
#               md5 779ff41622b2fb4ec91ed29c4a7db108
# QEMU invocation per tools/chain-regress.sh + '-drive sd.img,id=sd' +
# the env pair; the interactive command was:
#   mount -t ext4 /dev/mmcblk1 /mnt && /mnt/vc_session /mnt/loader.bin /mnt/fw.bin
#
# Determinism: the client transcript is byte-identical across all four
# boots except the single "driver mode:" line; TCG vs -icount are fully
# identical within a mode (model trace included); poll vs IRQ differ
# only in that line + which side services the same event set (32 model
# trace lines).  After the four boots: the chain-regress summaries
# (default envs + MESSI_RESPONDER=1, TCG and -icount) — the 1202-line
# flow byte-identical everywhere, the tree untouched by the client.

